      <categoryLink id="caa0a4d4-11a5-44c5-91a9-3b9e951cb7e6" name="Primarch" hidden="false" targetId="aa8f9cca-79d6-4483-b466-901fa59a2823" primary="false"><constraints><constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="ac394eef-241d-4ac0-aa91-1e6c9d7130d1" type="max" /></constraints></categoryLink></categoryLinks>
    <rules><rule id="ce16511e-8b46-5717-a5fb-2a43176622d4" name="The Battle Round" hidden="false"><description>1. Muster — flip Reload tokens, refresh Fleet Orders, declare Reactor Overloads, roll Initiative. 2. Movement — alternate one ship each, then one aircraft squadron each. 3. Shooting — alternate one ship or squadron each. 4. Ramming &amp; Boarding — alternate one ship each. 5. End of round — dogfights, then Critical Damage. A game lasts six rounds.</description></rule><rule id="5202b8be-9184-5bb6-b386-b8ff3066aed9" name="To Hit" hidden="false"><description>Roll a D6 per shot, hitting on 7 − BS. A natural 1 always misses and no modifier lowers the roll below 2+. Held station: broadsides +1 BS. Crippled −1, Depleted −1. Never above BS 5. Target is an Escort or Frigate that moved full Speed: −1. Target is a wreck: +1.</description></rule><rule id="30df1dfb-12e6-5312-a8b2-e27342212643" name="Void Shields" hidden="false"><description>While Void Shield Rating is above 0 the shields are Armour Value 12 and every hit strikes them. Roll 1D6 + Strength against AV 12; equal or better collapses one layer and does nothing else. There is no save. At VS 0 the shields are gone permanently and AP applies in full. Torpedoes, Melta Mines and Warp Lance Batteries bypass shields entirely; nothing else does.</description></rule><rule id="f578bce5-fdb6-5a9e-90db-bc8fda3f7357" name="Penetration" hidden="false"><description>Roll 1D6 + Strength against the Armour Value of the facing struck. Equal = Glancing Hit (1 Hull Point, no damage roll). Greater = Penetrating Hit (1 Hull Point and a Damage Table roll). At 6″ or less, Port, Starboard and Dorsal weapons improve AP one step — or gain Armourbane instead if their printed AP is already 1. Prow weapons get neither.</description></rule><rule id="4b9b9b43-1d58-544a-9d42-63873e7dce06" name="Ship Damage Table" hidden="false"><description>1 Held — nothing further. 2 Blaze — +1 Critical Damage. 3 Hull Breach — +1 Critical Damage. 4 Magazine Explosion — 1 Hull Point (2 with Triple Lance Batteries), +1 Critical Damage, and a random Port, Starboard or Dorsal system destroyed. 5 Engines Crippled — immobile, Snap Shots only; a second leaves it Adrift. 6 Reactor Struck — a Line Ship suffers a Catastrophic Explosion at once; a Capital Ship takes D3 Hull Points then detonates on a 6; a Gloriana or larger takes D3 and rolls 2D6, detonating if either shows a 6. Modifiers: AP 2 +1 · AP 1 +2 · Destroyer +3 (+2 vs Gloriana, Abyss, Phalanx) · Ramming +1 · Battleship target −1. A modified 7+ is Reactor Struck; below 1 counts as 1.</description></rule><rule id="bc12e5f5-0c84-5f16-9162-512bbb3753a5" name="Fleet Orders" hidden="false"><description>Only the Flagship issues orders, within 24″ Command range, and no test is needed. Three types — Command, Movement, Shooting — each up to the commander's rank per round: Captain 1, Named Character 2, Primarch 3. No ship takes two orders of the same type in a round. Ranks never combine and nothing adds to the allowance. Command: Damage Control, Focus Fire, Brace for Impact. Movement: All Ahead Full, Burn Retros, Evade. Shooting: Reload Ordnance, Return Fire, Overwatch.</description></rule><rule id="065e9f10-8022-5547-ae5c-0e1f0ac8c625" name="Movement" hidden="false"><description>A ship moves at least half its Speed and no more than 12″ (All Ahead Full excepted). One turn per round of 90°/180°/270°/360° up to the Turn value, and only after first moving a quarter of its Speed straight. Come About!: Escorts and Frigates may turn at any point in their move.</description></rule><rule id="219f1c03-fb3f-54ee-a274-0314176d5364" name="Ramming" hidden="false"><description>Free, and any ship may declare one against an enemy within 6″ of its prow. Roll a D6; the ram connects if it equals or beats the distance in inches. The target may Evade on 5+. On impact the target suffers one hit at Strength = the rammer's Prow AV, ignoring Void Shields, inflicting D6 Hull Points and rolling on the Damage Table at +1. The rammer loses D3. Survivors are Locked: neither may move, the rammer may not fire on its victim, and the victim fires back at −1 BS. Break Away on 5+.</description></rule><rule id="d368edea-e96a-5a1f-b22b-cf135a65abde" name="Boarding Actions" hidden="false"><description>Crew are the hit points of boarding. Declare the Crew committed and the delivery method; a ship always keeps 1 aboard. Every fighter rolls his own D6 with his own bonus. Starting with the boarders, players alternate nominating duels; the higher total fells its opponent and ties are re-rolled until decisive. Fight on until one side reaches 0 Crew or the boarders withdraw. Defenders reduced to 0 lose the ship — Capture or Scuttle.</description></rule><rule id="6404c86f-fff0-5f04-83fa-770ad9ee6db4" name="Attrition" hidden="false"><description>There is no Morale. Crippled — below half starting Hull Points: −1 BS and half Speed. Depleted — at half starting Crew or less: −1 BS. The two stack. Broken Fleet — once three quarters of a fleet's starting points are lost, it loses the battle at once.</description></rule><rule id="2af3f8f7-c450-57df-8168-72ef352ca814" name="Weapon Keywords" hidden="false"><description>Armourbane — 2D6 + Strength to penetrate at 6″ or less. Destroyer (D) — penetrates automatically and rolls at +3 (+2 vs Gloriana, Abyss, Phalanx); always at least Devastating (3); does not pass Void Shields. Devastating (X) — each hit costs X Hull Points, or 1 Void Shield Rating against live shields. Gets Hot — after the mount fires, on a D6 roll of 1 the firing ship loses 1 Hull Point. One Shot — fired once per battle. Reload (X) — X tokens after firing, one removed each Muster; the mount cannot fire while a token remains. Skyfire — full BS against aircraft. Twin-Linked — re-roll failed To Hit rolls. Volatile — an unmodified 1 To Hit resolves the attack against the firing ship.</description></rule></rules></forceEntry>
